{
  "sim_type": "excel",
  "title": "Link HDFC Bank's Three Statements and Pass the Balance Check",
  "scenario": "You're a junior analyst at a Mumbai research desk preparing a five-year model for HDFC Bank. The Inputs, P&L, schedules (capex, working capital, debt) are ready, but the balance sheet and cash flow remain partially blank. Your task: wire the schedules into the statements, close the loop with cash, and verify the balance check turns green for all five years.",
  "instructions": "Link the capex depreciation and debt interest into the P&L, populate the balance sheet from schedule sources with cash left blank, converge the schedules into the cash flow statement, then link closing cash back to the balance sheet and confirm the balance check formula passes.",
  "learning_objective": "Assemble a complete, balanced five-year three-statement model by linking schedules to statements, closing the cash loop, and deploying a balance check formula to verify integrity across all forecast years.",
  "hints": [
    "The balance sheet's cash line should reference the cash flow statement's closing cash — not a formula inside cash itself, just a link to another sheet.",
    "Retained earnings = opening reserves + PAT (from P&L) − dividends paid (PAT × payout ratio). Make sure PAT flows into *both* the balance sheet *and* the cash flow's starting line.",
    "The balance check is =IF(ABS(Total Assets − Total Liabilities & Equity)<0.5,\"OK\",\"CHECK\"). Place it one row below the balance sheet totals for each year. If it reads CHECK, trace Precedents on cash and reserves to find which link is broken."
  ],
